00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:02.159
We have a voicemail number.

00:00:02.159 --> 00:00:03.790
That number is two, one nine two.

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:10.790
David P here's an interesting question about
how I would handle a particular interpersonal

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:11.790
scenario.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:12.790
Take a listen.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:15.099
Uh, hi David.

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:24.070
Uh, I had a question, kind of a philosophical
question to ponder about AB.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:35.560
Um, and it's, um, if someone, uh, you know,
an acquaintance, uh, who is a big admirer

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:36.680
of yours.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:37.680
Okay.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:43.870
Uh, you found out later that they were rapist
and murderer, right?

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:47.410
How would you respond to that?

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:51.300
Would you shut them out completely?

00:00:51.300 --> 00:01:07.530
Um, would you, uh, try to, you know, get,
get further details on, on exactly what, what

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:08.579
they did?

00:01:08.579 --> 00:01:14.990
Uh, would you try to understand or what, I'm
just, I'm curious.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:17.200
Listen, I have no idea.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:18.649
This has never happened to me before.

00:01:18.649 --> 00:01:24.060
I've never found out that an acquaintance
or friend or something is a rapist or a murderer

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.009
and I don't know what would happen.

00:01:26.009 --> 00:01:28.249
I mean it's, I could give you some answer.

00:01:28.249 --> 00:01:30.929
I could say, Oh, I would definitely cut them
out of my life.

00:01:30.929 --> 00:01:33.079
I could never have contact with him again.

00:01:33.079 --> 00:01:36.759
Or I could say, you know, listen, I would
try to understand and if it was far enough

00:01:36.759 --> 00:01:41.360
in the past at the time when they were really
a different person than I, I have no idea.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:44.310
I think the details probably would matter.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:49.229
My guess is that there are people in our audience
who, listen, they're there.

00:01:49.229 --> 00:01:54.250
There must be people in our audience who are
acquainted with maybe not murderers, but,

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:58.469
um, more than likely, at least some people
in the audience, the audience is big enough

00:01:58.469 --> 00:02:01.040
where there's probably people acquainted with
rapists.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:02.040
I don't know.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:05.729
I'd be curious to hear from others what a,
it was like when something like that was revealed.

00:02:05.729 --> 00:02:06.729
I don't.

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:11.740
I think that, you know, this is like when
people say if I was on a plane and a terrorist

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:14.890
did X or Y, here's I would react.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:17.080
I don't think we know until we're in these
situations.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:21.040
I think there's so much in the details and
I wouldn't even pretend to be able to say

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.860
definitively what it is that I would do.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:24.980
Let me know what you think.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:28.100
If you've been in such a situation I would
be interested in hearing from you.

